// examples/hydramodem/basis.exsc -- the certificate driver: milestone M2
// of docs/design/modem.md, and the only file of its unit that names
// `Mundus`. It writes no WAV. For each of 137 words it writes the tone of
// each of the frame's 356 symbols as modulator.exsc's `tonus` decides it,
// one byte a symbol, 0 or 1: 137 x 356 = 48,772 bytes on standard output,
// which tests/programs/hydramodem_basis/ compares byte for byte with
// vendor/hydramodem-tx/symbola_basis.bin -- the same streams, reduced from
// 137 renders of HydraModem's own frame_tx (PROVENANCE.md there says how).
// Compiled with quantum.exsc and modulator.exsc, not emitte.exsc: the
// functions certified are the ones the WAV drivers use, unchanged.
//
// Byte 356 k + s is symbol s of word k. Word 0 is seventeen zero bytes.
// Word k = 1..136 has exactly wire bit i = k - 1 set: byte i / 8 under the
// mask 0x80 deorsum (i mod 8) -- MSB first across the wire, spec §14 entry
// 23's syndrome-basis numbering, walked the way entry23/probatio.exsc's
// `verte` walks it. No word is written in this file: each is derived from
// its index, and the mask is a one-hot byte moved by `deorsum 1`, so there
// is no variable shift and no division.
//
// Why 137 words and not 2^136. The map from a word's 136 bits to its 356
// tones is affine over GF(2) -- the CRC is affine, the code is a linear
// filter with zero state and zero tail, the interleaver is a permutation,
// one bit a symbol is the identity, preamble and sync are constants -- so
// S(f) = S(0) xor the xor of (S(e_i) xor S(0)) over the bits i set in f,
// and agreeing with the reference on these 137 words is agreeing on all
// 2^136 inputs, valid DeModFrames or not. GIVEN that affinity, for this
// code and for the reference's: it is argued from reading both
// (docs/design/modem.md D9 and section 7), not measured, exactly as entry
// 23's certificate is. None of the 137 is a valid DeModFrame, and each has
// a nonzero modem CRC (measured, all 137): the sixteen CRC bits that M1's
// three valid frames always carry as zeros are exercised here.
//
// `initium` returns 0 when every one of the 48,772 calls wrote its byte, 1
// otherwise. What the bytes are is the harness's to judge. The helpers write
// no `poscit`; their rows are inferred (spec §4.1 rule 5), as emitte.exsc's
// are, and for the same reason (docs/design/wire-codec.md finding 9).

// The 356 tones of the word w, in order, one byte each.
functio scribe_symbola(s: Scriptor, w: acies<u8, 17>) -> mensura {
    firma c: u16 = redundantia(w, 17);
    mutabilis n: mensura = 0;
    per y in 0..symbola {
        mutabilis t: u8 = 0;
        si tonus(w, c, y) eq 1 {
            t = 1;
        }
        n = n + s.scribe_octeto(t);
    }
    redde n;
}

// Words 1..136: for wire bit i = 0..135 of the zero word `nihil`, in order,
// set it with `aut`, write the word's tones, clear it again.
functio ambula(s: Scriptor, nihil: acies<u8, 17>) -> mensura {
    mutabilis w = nihil;
    mutabilis n: mensura = 0;
    per j in 0..17 {
        mutabilis m: u8 = 0x80;
        per k in 0..8 {
            w[j] = w[j] aut m;
            n = n + scribe_symbola(s, w);
            w[j] = w[j] aut m;
            m = m deorsum 1;
        }
    }
    redde n;
}

publica functio initium(m: Mundus) -> u8 {
    firma a = m.ambitus();
    sub ambitus = a;
    firma s = Scriptor.ad_exitum(a);
    // Seventeen zero bytes: every field of the frame 0, `signum` included.
    firma nihil = DeModFrame {
        signum: 0,
        versio: 0,
        genus: 0,
        numerus: 0,
        fons: 0,
        meta: 0,
        onus: 0,
        tempus: 0,
        cursus: 0
    } sicut acies<u8, 17>;
    mutabilis n: mensura = scribe_symbola(s, nihil);   // word 0
    n = n + ambula(s, nihil);                          // words 1..136
    si n ne 48772 {
        redde 1;
    }
    redde 0;
}
